<!--
  BlockML Core — primitive type branch

  FQN: org.blockml.type.PrimitiveType
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:btype="org.blockml.type"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.core">

  <idea>Branch for atomic scalar value types — pure type semantics, no stored data.</idea>

  <documentation>Abstract branch for built-in scalar ValueTypes. PrimitiveTypes describe semantics
    only — they never store concrete values. All values are stored exclusively in Properties.

    Numeric branch: org.blockml.type.Number (Integer, Decimal, Float). Textual branch:
    org.blockml.type.Text (FullyQualifiedName, Version, URL, URI, FilePath, MimeType, …).
    Boolean is its own branch — neither textual nor numeric.

    When a primitive value must exist as an Entity inside a composition or aggregation, use a
    concrete *Entity type (for example org.blockml.type.IntegerEntity) — not by adding a value
    member to the PrimitiveType.

    Invalid: &lt;type:Integer value="5"/&gt; — PrimitiveTypes cannot carry values.
    Valid: &lt;property name="count" type="Integer"&gt;&lt;value&gt;5&lt;/value&gt;&lt;/property&gt;

    See docs/17_type_system_bml.md — PrimitiveType · PrimitiveEntity.</documentation>
  <name>PrimitiveType</name>
  <type>btype:PrimitiveType</type>
  <baseType>core:ValueType</baseType>
  <abstract />

</block>
